<title>SWEDEN: Swedish Riksbank board meeting ends, no changes.</title>
<headline>Swedish Riksbank board meeting ends, no changes.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>A meeting of Sweden's central bank, the Riksbank, ended on Thursday morning with no changes announced to interest rates.</p>
<p>The bank's key repo rate currently stands at 4.10 percent while its other key rates, the deposit and lending rates, are 3.75 percent and 5.25 percent respectively.</p>
<p>The repo rate was last changed on December 17, when it was lowered by 25 basis points, while the other rates were last lowered on December 5.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
